---
// Privacy policy. Linked from the app (sign-in screen, Ask Dusty's AI notice)
// and from the App Store listing, so the URL /privacy must not change.
//
// Written from what the app actually does (dusty repo, 2026-11-03). When the
// app starts collecting something new, or a new company handles data (e.g.
// PostHog analytics), update this page and the App Store privacy label
// (dusty/docs/app-store-submission.md §4) together.
//
// Not reviewed by a lawyer. The retention periods (30-day restore window,
// 6 years for booking records) are what the code does; confirm them.
import TextPage from '../layouts/TextPage.astro';
import { company, contact } from '../data/site';
import { filled } from '../data/filled';

const number = filled(company.number);
const office = filled(company.registeredOffice);
const ico = filled(company.icoNumber);
---

<TextPage
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="How Dusty collects, uses and protects your personal data."
  updated="3 November 2026"
>
  <p class="mt-8">
    This policy explains what personal data Dusty collects when you use our app and website, why we collect it, who
    we share it with, how long we keep it, and your rights. Please read it alongside our <a href="/terms">terms</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="who-we-are">1. Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    Dusty is run by <strong>{company.legalName}</strong> (trading as {company.tradingName}), a company registered in
    England and Wales{number && <>, company number {number}</>}{office && <>, registered office {office}</>}. We are
    the data controller for the personal data described here. We are registered with the Information Commissioner's
    Office (ICO){ico && <>, registration number {ico}</>}.
  </p>
  <p>
    Questions about your data, or a request to use any of your rights: email
    <a href={`mailto:${contact.email}`}>{contact.email}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="what-we-collect">2. What we collect</h2>

  <h3>Everyone with an account</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Account details:</strong> your name, email address, password (stored encrypted by our authentication provider; we can't see it) and whether you're a customer or a cleaner.</li>
    <li><strong>Mobile number:</strong> verified by text message. It's used for calls about a booking through Dusty's own number, so the other person never sees your number.</li>
    <li><strong>Profile photo</strong>, if you add one.</li>
    <li><strong>Messages</strong> you send to other users in the app, and enquiries before a booking.</li>
    <li><strong>Reports and blocks</strong> you make, or that are made about you.</li>
    <li><strong>Device information:</strong> a push notification token so we can send you notifications, and crash reports (the type of phone, app version and what went wrong, not who you are).</li>
    <li><strong>What you send us</strong> when you contact support.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Customers</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Your homes:</strong> address, postcode, type of property, number of bedrooms and bathrooms, access instructions, pets, and what products and equipment you have.</li>
    <li><strong>Bookings:</strong> the service, date and time, price, notes and any photos you add for your cleaner, and the booking's history.</li>
    <li><strong>Payment:</strong> your card is entered into Stripe's secure payment form. Stripe stores it; we only see the card type, last four digits and expiry date.</li>
    <li><strong>What you type to Ask Dusty</strong>, our AI booking assistant (see <a href="#ai">section 5</a>).</li>
    <li><strong>Reviews</strong> you write, and <strong>ratings</strong> cleaners give you after a clean (four yes/no questions, such as whether the home was ready on time).</li>
    <li><strong>Points and referrals:</strong> your points balance and history, and your referral code.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Cleaners</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Work profile:</strong> your bio, hourly rate, services, the area you cover (a base location and distance), working hours and days off.</li>
    <li><strong>Verification documents:</strong> photos of your ID, right to work and proof of address, the dates on them, and our team's decision.</li>
    <li><strong>Insurance certificate</strong>, if you upload one.</li>
    <li><strong>Payouts:</strong> you set up payouts with Stripe, which collects your bank details and identity information directly. We see whether payouts are set up, not your full bank details.</li>
    <li><strong>Jobs:</strong> bookings, bids, start and finish times, problems you report on a job, and your earnings.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>What we don't collect</h3>
  <p>
    The app doesn't read your phone's location. It works from the postcode of your home or your work area. We don't
    record calls, use advertising trackers, or sell your data.
  </p>

  <h3>Website</h3>
  <p>
    If you join our waitlist on getdusty.co.uk, we collect your name, email address and town through Google Forms. The
    website doesn't use cookies or analytics.
  </p>

  <h2 id="how-we-use-it">3. How we use it, and our legal basis</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>What we do</th><th>Legal basis (UK GDPR)</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>Create your account, match customers with cleaners, run bookings, take payments and pay cleaners, send booking notifications and emails</td>
        <td>Contract: we need it to provide the service you signed up for</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Check cleaners' identity and documents before they can take bookings</td>
        <td>Legitimate interests: keeping customers safe in their homes</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Automatically block contact details and offensive words in messages; look into reports; suspend accounts that break our terms</td>
        <td>Legitimate interests: safety, and stopping fraud and payments outside the app</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Send what you type to Ask Dusty to our AI provider</td>
        <td>Consent, which the app asks for before your first message. You can book with the form instead</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Keep booking and payment records</td>
        <td>Legal obligation: company and tax record-keeping</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Fix crashes and improve the app</td>
        <td>Legitimate interests: a reliable app</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>
    <strong>Our team reading messages.</strong> Messages are private between you and the other person. Our team only
    opens a conversation for a reason: a report, a safety concern, a payment dispute or a legal request. Every time
    they do, it's logged.
  </p>

  <h2 id="sharing">4. Who we share it with</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>The other person on a booking.</strong> A cleaner you book sees your name, the home's address and
    access instructions, your notes and photos, and your rating as a customer. A customer sees a cleaner's name,
    photo, bio, rate, reviews and approximate distance. Neither sees the other's phone number or email address.
  </p>
  <p><strong>Companies that run parts of Dusty for us.</strong> They may only use your data to provide their service to us:</p>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Company</th><th>What for</th><th>Where</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Supabase</td><td>Database, file storage and sign-in</td><td>EU</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Fly.io</td><td>Our servers</td><td>UK (London)</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Stripe</td><td>Card payments, and cleaners' payouts and identity checks for payouts</td><td>UK, EU and USA</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Anthropic</td><td>The AI behind Ask Dusty, and the one-line explanation of why a cleaner was matched</td><td>USA</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Twilio</td><td>Texting verification codes, and connecting calls through Dusty's number</td><td>USA</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Resend</td><td>Sending emails</td><td>USA / EU</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Expo and Apple</td><td>Push notifications</td><td>USA</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Sentry</td><td>Crash reports</td><td>EU (Germany)</td></tr>
      <tr><td>postcodes.io</td><td>Turning a postcode into a map position (only the postcode is sent)</td><td>UK</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Google</td><td>Website waitlist form</td><td>USA / EU</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>
    Where data goes outside the UK, it's protected by the safeguards UK law requires, such as the UK–US data bridge or
    the ICO's International Data Transfer Addendum.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Others, only when we have to:</strong> the police or other authorities when the law requires it, our
    professional advisers, or a buyer if the business is ever sold (they'd be bound by this policy).
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai">5. Ask Dusty and AI</h2>
  <p>
    Ask Dusty lets you describe the clean you need in your own words. To understand it, we send
    <strong>Anthropic</strong> (the company behind the Claude AI) what you type in Ask Dusty, plus your home's type
    and number of bedrooms. We don't send your name, email, phone number or address. The app asks your permission
    before your first message, and you can always book with the form instead, which sends nothing you type to an AI.
  </p>
  <p>
    When we show you a match, we also send Anthropic the cleaner's first name, rating, rate and distance, so it can
    write one sentence about why they suit your booking.
  </p>
  <p>
    Anthropic processes this for us under a data processing agreement. It doesn't use it to train its AI. The AI
    suggests a cleaner; it never books one or makes a decision about you. You and the cleaner both choose.
  </p>

  <h2 id="retention">6. How long we keep it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>While you have an account,</strong> we keep what's needed to run it.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>When you delete your account</strong> (Account → Delete account in the app): your account is hidden
      and you're signed out straight away, and a cleaner's ID and verification documents are deleted that day. You
      have <strong>30 days</strong> to change your mind by signing in. After 30 days we erase your account.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Booking and payment records are kept for 6 years</strong>, because UK company and tax law requires
      it. When your account is erased, we remove your name, photo, homes and other personal details from those
      records and keep only what the law needs. Messages about a booking are kept with it, in case of a dispute,
      and erased when the 6 years are up. Messages that weren't about a booking are erased with your account.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Legal hold:</strong> if we're dealing with a dispute, claim or legal request involving you, we may keep
      the relevant data until it's resolved.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Crash reports</strong> are deleted automatically within 90 days.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="rights">7. Your rights</h2>
  <p>Under UK data protection law you can ask us to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>give you a copy of your personal data</li>
    <li>correct anything that's wrong</li>
    <li>delete your data (you can also do this yourself in the app)</li>
    <li>restrict or object to how we use it</li>
    <li>give you your data in a format you can move to another service</li>
    <li>withdraw your consent for Ask Dusty, by not using it. Tell us if you'd like the setting on your phone reset</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Email <a href={`mailto:${contact.email}`}>{contact.email}</a>. We'll reply within one month. It's free.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you're unhappy with how we've handled your data, you can complain to the Information Commissioner's Office at
    <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/">ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint</a> or on 0303 123 1113. We'd
    appreciate the chance to put it right first.
  </p>

  <h2 id="security">8. Security</h2>
  <p>
    Data is encrypted in transit and at rest. Verification documents are kept in private storage that only our
    verification team can open. Access inside Dusty is limited to the people who need it, and staff access to
    private messages is logged.
  </p>

  <h2 id="age">9. Age</h2>
  <p>Dusty is for people aged 18 and over. We don't knowingly collect data from anyone younger.</p>

  <h2 id="changes">10. Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If we change this policy, we'll update the date at the top. If the change matters, such as a new use of your
    data, we'll tell you in the app or by email first.
  </p>
</TextPage>
